        <h2>How to Reserve a Self Drive Car Rental</h2>
        <div>
            <div class="section">
                <ul>
                    <li>  After contacting any sales staff from the company and decide to book a car: </li>
                    <li>  1) Send the required documents (soft-copy) to AJDavao88@gmail.com for assessment. </li>
                    <li>  2) Wait for the advise for the approval and availability.</li>
                    <li>  3) Once approved, settle the required reservation fee.</li>
                    <li>  4) Booking confirmation will be sent thru email.</li>

                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="section">
                <h3> Self Drive Rental Requirements </h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>   Car rental company requires proper identification for self drive rentals. Below are the basic requirements.</li>
                    <li>    1) Driver’s License</li>
                    <li>    2) Government Issued IDs</li>
                    <li>    3) Proof of residence (House bill, Water bill, hotel accommodation)</li>
                    <li>    4) Air-ticket – if applicable</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="section">
                <h3> Releasing Self Drive Vehicle </h3>
                <p>
                    When approved and booked, you are now ready to pickup your requested vehicle. The rental company have the option to deliver at the airport or to where you stay with minimal delivery charge applies. Delivery charge to airport and downtown areas is P300. Delivery charge will vary for areas outside downtown and outside the city.
                </p>

                <ul>
                    <li> There are few things to check and comply for self drive rentals. </li>
                    <li>1) Check the general appearance of the vehicle: body dents, paint scratches, windshield and windows, interior damages, tires, rims. </li>
                    <li>2) Driving condition of the vehicle: Fuel, Brake, lights, oil and fluids, coolant, steering, unwanted engine sound, body noise.  </li>
                </ul>

                <ul>

                    <li>Need to comply the following: </li>
                    <li>1) Signed rental contract. </li>
                    <li>2) full payment and damage deposit (cash) </li>

                </ul>
                <p>

                    Follow what is agreed in the contract to avoid inconveniences. If you have questions and confusion , immediately ask for clarification. The rental company is flexible as long as terms and needs are discussed accordingly.

                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="section">
                <h3>
                    Returning Self Drive Rental Vehicle
                </h3>
                <p>
                    The car rental company has the option to pickup the rented vehicle at the airport or any place requested by the renter. Minimal charge of P300 applies for airport or Davao downtown area. Pickup fee for other areas outside downtown or out of the city will vary.
                </p>

                <ul>
                    <li>Things to check: </li>
                    <li>1) Appearance : Dents and scratches, windshield, tires, Interiors, etc. </li>
                    <li>2) Driving : Fuel </li>
                    <li>3) Contract and additional charges if applicable. </li>
                    <li>4) Refund of cash deposit. </li>

                </ul>  
                <p>
                    Damages incurred during the use of the vehicle will be assessed accordingly and estimated repair cost shall be paid by the renter.
                    Cash deposit will be refunded once damages is settled.
                </p>
            </div>
          

        </div>


    @if (ViewBag.CtaBox != null)
